 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? For oil paintings, usually two to three weeks is ideal. Let it dry completely in between layers, or the colours won't mix properly. Then you' missed the window. Oil paints take a long time to dry, and if they're mixed with resin, they slow down even more. Yes, a fast dry varnish can be used, but it' only a stopgap. Proper curing takes time. It' touch dry in year or two, but the resin finish won't be fully cured. For a present, I'd leave it another six months before varnishing.",
